  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_rose_of_jericho_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>the rose of Jericho, a small annual cruciferous plant (Anastatica hierochuntina), the dried fronds of which unfold under the influence of moisture (OED s.v. rose of Jericho) | Rose of Jericho, a small annual cruciferous plant (Anastatica hierochuntina), native to the arid deserts of South-west Asia and North-east Africa, the dried fronds of which unfold under the influence of moisture (OED s.v. Mary 1c, rose of Jericho) | probably St. Mary's herb (costmary), used in medicine and to flavour ale (OED s.v. herb 7b) rather than St. Mary's flower, Rose of Jericho (OED s.v. Mary 1c)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
